§ `Tests of regulation 6: scoring mobility activities`

-- Mobility 1b 4 + 2a 0 = 4; 1b 4 + 2b 4 = 8; 1d 10 + 2a 0 = 10; 1f 12 + 2a 0 = 12; 1d 10 + 2b 4 = 14; 1f 12 + 2f 12 = 24.
`mobility four points` MEANS `the descriptors that apply to C in the mobility activities` WITH `for planning and following journeys` IS `mobility 1b`, `for moving around` IS `mobility 2a`
`mobility eight points` MEANS `the descriptors that apply to C in the mobility activities` WITH `for planning and following journeys` IS `mobility 1b`, `for moving around` IS `mobility 2b`
`mobility ten points` MEANS `the descriptors that apply to C in the mobility activities` WITH `for planning and following journeys` IS `mobility 1d`, `for moving around` IS `mobility 2a`
`mobility twelve points` MEANS `the descriptors that apply to C in the mobility activities` WITH `for planning and following journeys` IS `mobility 1f`, `for moving around` IS `mobility 2a`
`mobility fourteen points` MEANS `the descriptors that apply to C in the mobility activities` WITH `for planning and following journeys` IS `mobility 1d`, `for moving around` IS `mobility 2b`
`mobility twenty-four points` MEANS `the descriptors that apply to C in the mobility activities` WITH `for planning and following journeys` IS `mobility 1f`, `for moving around` IS `mobility 2f`
`mobility none selected for moving around` MEANS `the descriptors that apply to C in the mobility activities` WITH `for planning and following journeys` IS `mobility 1f`, `for moving around` IS `no descriptor of mobility activity 2 applies`

#ASSERT `reg 6(1): the score C obtains in mobility activities` `mobility four points` EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `reg 6(1): the score C obtains in mobility activities` `mobility eight points` EQUALS JUST 8
#ASSERT `reg 6(1): the score C obtains in mobility activities` `mobility ten points` EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `reg 6(1): the score C obtains in mobility activities` `mobility twelve points` EQUALS JUST 12
#ASSERT `reg 6(1): the score C obtains in mobility activities` `mobility fourteen points` EQUALS JUST 14
#ASSERT `reg 6(1): the score C obtains in mobility activities` `mobility twenty-four points` EQUALS JUST 24
#ASSERT `reg 6(1): the score C obtains in mobility activities` `mobility none selected for moving around` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `reg 6(3): C's level of ability to carry out mobility activities` TRUE (JUST 4) EQUALS JUST `neither limited ability nor severely limited ability`
#ASSERT `reg 6(3): C's level of ability to carry out mobility activities` TRUE (JUST 8) EQUALS JUST `limited ability`
#ASSERT `reg 6(3): C's level of ability to carry out mobility activities` TRUE (JUST 10) EQUALS JUST `limited ability`
#ASSERT `reg 6(3): C's level of ability to carry out mobility activities` TRUE (JUST 12) EQUALS JUST `severely limited ability`
#ASSERT `reg 6(3): C's level of ability to carry out mobility activities` FALSE (JUST 12) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 6(3): C's level of ability to carry out mobility activities` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests of regulation 7: the required period`

-- A prescribed date of 15 June 2025. The 3 months ending with it: 16 March to 15 June 2025 (16 + 30 + 31 + 15 = 92 days).
-- The 9 months beginning the day after: 16 June 2025 to 15 March 2026 (15 + 31 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 30 + 31 + 31 + 28 + 15 = 273 days). 92 + 273 = 365.
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(a)(ii): the required period for any other claim` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15))'s `the first day of the 3 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 3 16
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(a)(ii): the required period for any other claim` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15))'s `the last day of the 3 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 6 15
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(a)(ii): the required period for any other claim` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15))'s `the first day of the 9 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 6 16
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(a)(ii): the required period for any other claim` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15))'s `the last day of the 9 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `reg 7(3): the number of days of the required period` (`reg 7(3)(a)(ii): the required period for any other claim` (YearMonthDay 2025 6 15)) EQUALS 365

-- (a)(i): previous award ended 10 March 2025, new claim made 20 June 2025.
-- 3 months ending 10 March 2025: 11 December 2024 to 10 March 2025. 9 months beginning with 20 June 2025: to 19 March 2026.
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(a)(i): the required period for a claim after an interval under regulation 15 or 15A` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 20))'s `the first day of the 3 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2024 12 11
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(a)(i): the required period for a claim after an interval under regulation 15 or 15A` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 20))'s `the last day of the 3 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 3 10
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(a)(i): the required period for a claim after an interval under regulation 15 or 15A` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 20))'s `the first day of the 9 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 6 20
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(a)(i): the required period for a claim after an interval under regulation 15 or 15A` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 6 20))'s `the last day of the 9 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 3 19

-- (b)(i): prescribed date 10 March 2025, day of the award 1 April 2025: 3 months as above; 9 months beginning 2 April 2025, to 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(b)(i): the required period for a day of an award in the 3 months after a claim for the purpose of regulation 15 or 15A` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1))'s `the first day of the 3 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2024 12 11
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(b)(i): the required period for a day of an award in the 3 months after a claim for the purpose of regulation 15 or 15A` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1))'s `the first day of the 9 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 4 2
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(b)(i): the required period for a day of an award in the 3 months after a claim for the purpose of regulation 15 or 15A` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1))'s `the last day of the 9 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 1 1

-- (b)(ii): day of the award 1 April 2025: 3 months ending 1 April 2025 begin 2 January 2025; 9 months from 2 April 2025 to 1 January 2026.
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(b)(ii): the required period for a day of an award in any other case` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1))'s `the first day of the 3 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 1 2
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(b)(ii): the required period for a day of an award in any other case` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1))'s `the last day of the 3 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 4 1
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(b)(ii): the required period for a day of an award in any other case` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1))'s `the first day of the 9 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 4 2
#ASSERT (`reg 7(3)(b)(ii): the required period for a day of an award in any other case` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 1))'s `the last day of the 9 months` EQUALS YearMonthDay 2026 1 1

§ `Tests of regulation 7: which descriptor applies`

-- Candidates from activity 1 (preparing food): 1a 0 points, 1b 2, 1c 2, 1e 4. The required period is taken as 100 days
-- so that "over 50%" is "more than 50 days".
`1a for 70 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1a`, 70
`1a for 40 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1a`, 40
`1b for 60 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1b`, 60
`1b for 51 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1b`, 51
`1b for 50 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1b`, 50
`1b for 30 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1b`, 30
`1b for 26 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1b`, 26
`1b for 25 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1b`, 25
`1b for no days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1b`, 0
`1c for 70 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1c`, 70
`1c for 21 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1c`, 21
`1e for 55 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1e`, 55
`1e for 30 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1e`, 30
`1e for 25 days` MEANS `a descriptor with the days on which it is satisfied` OF `row for daily living 1e`, 25

-- reg 7(1)(a): one descriptor over 50% of the days. 51 of 100 is over; exactly 50 is not.
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(a): the descriptor satisfied on over 50% of the days, where one is` (LIST `1b for 60 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1b`
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(a): the descriptor satisfied on over 50% of the days, where one is` (LIST `1b for 51 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1b`
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(a): the descriptor satisfied on over 50% of the days, where one is` (LIST `1b for 50 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- One over 50% among others that are not: still limb (a).
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(a): the descriptor satisfied on over 50% of the days, where one is` (LIST `1b for 30 days`, `1e for 55 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1e`
-- Two over 50%: not limb (a).
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(a): the descriptor satisfied on over 50% of the days, where one is` (LIST `1b for 60 days`, `1e for 55 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS NOTHING

-- reg 7(1)(b): two or more each over 50%: the higher or highest points. 1e (4) beats 1b (2).
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(b): the descriptor scoring the highest points, where two or more are each satisfied on over 50% of the days` (LIST `1b for 60 days`, `1e for 55 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1e`
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(b): the descriptor scoring the highest points, where two or more are each satisfied on over 50% of the days` (LIST `1e for 55 days`, `1b for 60 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1e`
-- A 0-point descriptor over 50% still takes part in limb (b): 1b (2) beats 1a (0).
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(b): the descriptor scoring the highest points, where two or more are each satisfied on over 50% of the days` (LIST `1a for 70 days`, `1b for 60 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1b`
-- Only one over 50%: not limb (b).
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(b): the descriptor scoring the highest points, where two or more are each satisfied on over 50% of the days` (LIST `1b for 60 days`, `1e for 30 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS NOTHING

-- reg 7(1)(c)(i): none over 50%, two or more others together over 50%: the one satisfied for the greatest proportion.
-- 1a 40 (0 points, left out), 1b 30, 1e 25: 30 + 25 = 55 > 50, and 1b is satisfied for more days, though 1e scores more.
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(c): the descriptor that applies where none is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` (LIST `1a for 40 days`, `1b for 30 days`, `1e for 25 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1b`
-- (c)(ii): the same proportion: 1b 30 and 1e 30 (60 > 50): the higher points, 1e.
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(c): the descriptor that applies where none is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` (LIST `1b for 30 days`, `1e for 30 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1e`
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(c): the descriptor that applies where none is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` (LIST `1e for 30 days`, `1b for 30 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1e`
-- A 0-point descriptor is left out of the addition: 1a 40 + 1b 30 would be 70, but 1b alone is not "two or more".
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(c): the descriptor that applies where none is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` (LIST `1a for 40 days`, `1b for 30 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Boundary of the sum: 25 + 25 = 50 is not over 50%; 26 + 25 = 51 is.
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(c): the descriptor that applies where none is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` (LIST `1b for 25 days`, `1e for 25 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(c): the descriptor that applies where none is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` (LIST `1b for 26 days`, `1e for 25 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1b`
-- A descriptor satisfied on no day does not count as one of the "two or more": 1e 30 + 1b 0 is one descriptor.
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(c): the descriptor that applies where none is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` (LIST `1b for no days`, `1e for 30 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 1e 30 + 1c 21 = 51 > 50: two descriptors, 1e for more days.
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(c): the descriptor that applies where none is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` (LIST `1e for 30 days`, `1c for 21 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1e`
-- Limb (c) does not apply when a descriptor is over 50%.
#ASSERT `reg 7(1)(c): the descriptor that applies where none is satisfied on over 50% but two or more together are` (LIST `1b for 60 days`, `1e for 30 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS NOTHING

-- reg 7(1) as a whole: (a), then (b), then (c); NOTHING where none selects a descriptor (not covered).
#ASSERT `reg 7(1): the descriptor which applies to C in relation to the activity` (LIST `1b for 60 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1b`
#ASSERT `reg 7(1): the descriptor which applies to C in relation to the activity` (LIST `1b for 60 days`, `1e for 55 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1e`
#ASSERT `reg 7(1): the descriptor which applies to C in relation to the activity` (LIST `1a for 40 days`, `1b for 30 days`, `1e for 25 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1b`
#ASSERT `reg 7(1): the descriptor which applies to C in relation to the activity` (LIST `1b for 30 days`, `1e for 30 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1e`
#ASSERT `reg 7(1): the descriptor which applies to C in relation to the activity` (LIST `1a for 40 days`, `1b for 30 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 7(1): the descriptor which applies to C in relation to the activity` (LIST `1b for 50 days`) `of` 100 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 7(1): the descriptor which applies to C in relation to the activity` EMPTY `of` 100 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Two descriptors that score alike and are both over 50%: the text does not choose one; the first listed is taken, and the points are the same.
#ASSERT (`reg 7(1): the descriptor which applies to C in relation to the activity` (LIST `1b for 60 days`, `1c for 70 days`) `of` 100) EQUALS JUST `row for daily living 1b`
#ASSERT `reg 7(2): the descriptor is satisfied on the day` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 7(2): the descriptor is satisfied on the day` FALSE)

§ `Tests of regulations 8 to 11`

-- reg 8(1)
#ASSERT `reg 8(1): the Secretary of State may require C to provide the information or evidence` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(1): the Secretary of State may require C to provide the information or evidence` FALSE)

-- reg 8(2): one month from the request of 10 March 2025 ends on 10 April 2025.
#ASSERT `reg 8(2): the last day for providing the information or evidence` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) NOTHING EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 4 10
-- A longer period the Secretary of State considers reasonable extends the time.
#ASSERT `reg 8(2): the last day for providing the information or evidence` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 5 1)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 5 1
-- A "longer" date that is not longer leaves one month.
#ASSERT `reg 8(2): the last day for providing the information or evidence` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20)) EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 4 10
-- Month-end request: 31 January 2025 plus one month is 28 February 2025 (clamped; fork F-1).
#ASSERT `reg 8(2): the last day for providing the information or evidence` (YearMonthDay 2025 1 31) NOTHING EQUALS YearMonthDay 2025 2 28
-- Provided on the last day: in time. The day after: not.
#ASSERT `reg 8(2): C provided the information or evidence in time` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 4 10))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(2): C provided the information or evidence in time` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 4 11)))
#ASSERT `reg 8(2): C provided the information or evidence in time` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 10) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2025 3 11))
-- Never provided: not in time.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(2): C provided the information or evidence in time` (YearMonthDay 2025 4 10) NOTHING)

-- reg 8(3): fails without good reason: a negative determination must be made.
#ASSERT `reg 8(3): a negative determination must be made in relation to the component to which the failure related` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(3): a negative determination must be made in relation to the component to which the failure related` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(3): a negative determination must be made in relation to the component to which the failure related` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 8(3): a negative determination must be made in relation to the component to which the failure related` TRUE TRUE)

-- reg 9(1)
#ASSERT `reg 9(1): C may be required to take part in a consultation` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 9(1): C may be required to take part in a consultation` FALSE)

-- reg 9(3): notice sent 1 March 2025 for a consultation on 8 March 2025 is 7 days in advance: enough. 7 March is 6 days: not enough.
-- (day sent, day of consultation, in writing on paper, sent electronically, C agreed to electronic correspondence, C agreed to a shorter period)
#ASSERT `reg 9(3): regulation 9(2) can apply because the notice requirement is met` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 8) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 9(3): regulation 9(2) can apply because the notice requirement is met` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 7) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `reg 9(3): regulation 9(2) can apply because the notice requirement is met` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 7) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Electronic notice is written notice only where C agreed to correspondence that way.
#ASSERT `reg 9(3): regulation 9(2) can apply because the notice requirement is met` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 9(3): regulation 9(2) can apply because the notice requirement is met` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- No written notice at all, and no agreement to short notice: not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 9(3): regulation 9(2) can apply because the notice requirement is met` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 20) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- C's agreement to a shorter period is enough on its own (limb (b)).
#ASSERT `reg 9(3): regulation 9(2) can apply because the notice requirement is met` (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 2) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

-- reg 9(2) with (5): (approved person, C failed, Secretary of State satisfied of good reason, notice requirement met)
#ASSERT `reg 9(2): a negative determination must be made because C failed to attend or participate` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 9(2): a negative determination must be made because C failed to attend or participate` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 9(2): a negative determination must be made because C failed to attend or participate` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 9(2): a negative determination must be made because C failed to attend or participate` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 9(2): a negative determination must be made because C failed to attend or participate` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- reg 10
#ASSERT `reg 10: regulation 10 requires this matter to be taken into account in determining good reason` `C's state of health at the relevant time`
#ASSERT `reg 10: regulation 10 requires this matter to be taken into account in determining good reason` `the nature of any disability that C has`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 10: regulation 10 requires this matter to be taken into account in determining good reason` `any other matter`)

-- reg 11: any reason, but not work or voluntary work, once a level has been determined.
#ASSERT `reg 11: the Secretary of State may determine afresh whether C continues to have limited or severely limited ability, for this reason` TRUE `any other reason`
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 11: the Secretary of State may determine afresh whether C continues to have limited or severely limited ability, for this reason` TRUE `C is doing work for payment or in expectation of payment`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 11: the Secretary of State may determine afresh whether C continues to have limited or severely limited ability, for this reason` TRUE `C is doing voluntary work`)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 11: the Secretary of State may determine afresh whether C continues to have limited or severely limited ability, for this reason` FALSE `any other reason`)
